    "body": "## Security/privacy impact\n\nPR #198 correctly made new STOMP CONNECT attempts honor the JWT `auth_version`, but a WebSocket session that had already connected before a password reset/change or account suspension could keep its existing broker subscriptions. With no further inbound frame required, that stale connection could continue receiving private chat, notification or live-tracking MESSAGE frames until the socket naturally disappeared.\n\nThat made the realtime channel weaker than the REST bearer boundary: credential invalidation stopped new REST requests and new WebSocket CONNECTs, but did not reliably stop protected data delivery to an already-established subscription.\n\n## Fix\n\n- bind every successful STOMP CONNECT session id to the authenticated account email and exact `auth_version`, without retaining the raw JWT;\n- revalidate the registered session/principal pair, `ACTIVE` account status and current `auth_version` on every later inbound STOMP frame;\n- remove stale session bindings on disconnect and when stale/mismatched state is detected;\n- add a client outbound interceptor that reloads account state immediately before every broker `MESSAGE` and drops delivery fail-closed when the session is unknown, the account is suspended/missing, or `auth_version` changed;\n- keep CONNECT_ACK/control frames unaffected so normal protocol establishment/teardown remains intact;\n- preserve existing chat/tracking participant authorization, notification routing, client-SEND denial and inbound abuse limits.\n\nThis intentionally does not claim an instantaneous physical TCP/WebSocket disconnect at the exact credential-change transaction. The security boundary is that protected realtime MESSAGE delivery stops and subsequent inbound frames are rejected once current account state no longer matches the credential-bound session.\n\n## Tests\n\n- unit coverage proves CONNECT stores the exact session credential identity;\n- stale `auth_version` and suspended established sessions are rejected on subsequent inbound frames;\n- outbound MESSAGE delivery succeeds only for a registered ACTIVE/current session;\n- stale, suspended and unknown outbound sessions are dropped before delivery and stale bindings are removed;\n- non-MESSAGE protocol frames remain untouched;\n- password-recovery runtime smoke now establishes a real STOMP session before password reset, keeps that same socket open across the reset, and requires the next frame on that established session to be rejected after `auth_version` increments;\n- existing runtime checks still require old-token REST access and new STOMP CONNECT rejection plus successful CONNECT with the newly issued token.\n\nDocumentation now records the credential-bound WebSocket lifecycle in both account/session and WebSocket security contracts.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after every relevant check on the exact PR head SHA is green. Revalidate the exact head, review threads and current `master` immediately before merge. If `master` moves, integrate it and rerun checks. Merge with a merge commit guarded by the checked head SHA, then verify merge parents and all post-merge push workflows before starting another slice.",
